                    <h2 class="sub">                    Multi-Pattern Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The CMH8C is a multipattern large-diaphragm FET condenser. It is the tripolar version of the company&#8217;s CMH8A/CMH8B.</p><p>Like the other mics in this series, it uses a one-inch, 3-micron capsule, FET circuitry, and a transformer-coupled output. It retains the pad and high-pass filter switches of the CMH8B, and adds a third switch for pattern selection (Omni, Fig-8, Cardioid).</p><p>A dual-layer mesh protects the capsule. The aluminum body has a &#8220;champagne silver&#8221; finish.</p><p>The mic ships with HM8 hardmount and A3 plastic hardcase.<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Superlux/CMH8C">Superlux CMH8C</a></p>
